> Is the intention really to make players regret their choices?

Certainly.  Nethack is a game that has some extremely
limited resources with other resources at other levels
of availability.  Skills slots are for some classes extremely
limited.

The intent appears to be to force players to plan ahead.
Noting the strategies used by regular ascenders this
design intent is clearly effective.

The ability to enhance skills happens much more often
than the availability to enhance them.  It calls for much
planning ahead.  While a few skill slots can be spent as
emergency points for early survival, doing so will make
the later game more difficult in many cases.  Learn to
survive the early game with fewer resources and the
later game has fewer restrictions.

> Then my
> intention is to make players stick with their choices for a while, not
