Inconsistant with a wide assortment of roguelike
features.  It's a cool idea and go ahead and implement
it if you want, but it won't be adopted by the DevTeam.

> If the skill system is fully automated, then does it not follow that
> it should make efficient use of the available resources?

The reason it's manual is to give players options.

On the other hand automating makes it more like real
life.  Tha'ts generally not a goal in roguelikes.


